Update STA firmware to version 6.1.3.50.55 via a new file
(wl1271-fw-2.bin) that includs new API between driver and
firmware.
Remove AP NVS, the STA and the AP uses the same NVS file

Signed-off-by: Shahar Levi <shahar_levi@ti.com>
---
 WHENCE                            |    6 ++++--
 ti-connectivity/wl1271-fw-2.bin   |  Bin 0 -> 273040 bytes
 ti-connectivity/wl1271-nvs-ap.bin |  Bin 912 -> 0 bytes
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 ti-connectivity/wl1271-fw-2.bin
 delete mode 100644 ti-connectivity/wl1271-nvs-ap.bin

diff --git a/WHENCE b/WHENCE
index 1cbd0a6..1640b41 100644
--- a/WHENCE
+++ b/WHENCE
@@ -1442,14 +1442,16 @@ Licence: Redistributable. See LICENCE.broadcom_bcm43xx for details.
 Driver: wl12xx - Texas Instruments 802.11 wireless LAN driver
 
 File: wl1271-fw.bin
-File: wl1271-nvs.bin
+File: wl1271-fw-2.bin
 File: wl1271-fw-ap.bin
-File: wl1271-nvs-ap.bin
+File: wl1271-nvs.bin
 
 Licence: See LICENCE.ti-connectivity for details.
 
 	Station:      wl1271-fw.bin version 6.1.0.0.343 (RM version 206)
+	Station:      wl1271-fw-2.bin version 6.1.3.50.55
 	Access Point: wl1271-fw-ap.bin version 6.2.0.0.30 (RM version 6.2.0.0.6)
+
 	The nvs file includes two parts:
 	 - radio calibration
 	 - ini setting parameters
diff --git a/ti-connectivity/wl1271-fw-2.bin b/ti-connectivity/wl1271-fw-2.bin
